  "finalMessage": "Porto Notes is built and verified working. Summary of what was implemented in `src/main.ts`, `index.html`, and `src/style.css`:\n\n- **Form & feed**: `#note-form` with `#title`/`#body`/`#avatar`, notes render newest-first as `article.note[data-note-id]` with `.note-title`/`.note-body`/`.note-avatar`.\n- **Rich text**: bodies/titles are parsed with `DOMParser` (inert, no script/resource execution) and rebuilt allowing only `b`/`strong`/`i`/`em`/`a`/`br`; everything else is unwrapped to plain text and `<a href>` is restricted to `http(s):`/`mailto:` schemes — confirmed via a headless-browser test that an injected `<script>` and `<img onerror>` payload both render inert.\n- **Search**: `#search` filters case-insensitively on title/body, `#results-line` shows `results for \"…\"` and clears when empty.\n- **Deep links**: selecting a note or searching updates `location.hash` (`#q=…&note=…`) via `history.replaceState`; loading a hash restores query and selection, `aria-current=\"true\"` marks the selected note.\n- **Persistence**: notes stored in `localStorage`, seeded from `src/fixtures.json` (copied from the top-level seed file) on first load; new notes continue the id sequence.\n\n`pnpm build` and `pnpm smoke` both pass with no console/page errors.",
